# Super Admin ↔ Seller Admin notifications

Any Super Admin action that affects a seller (approve, reject, revision, listing restrict, warn, restrict, ban, deactivate, unrestrict, unban, and similar) MUST notify the seller admin inbox.

Any seller-admin action Super Admin oversees (new listing, resubmit/update while in review, delete listing, and similar) MUST notify the Super Admin inbox.

Do not drop unread notifications. Do not cap seller/SA inboxes at 50. Use `appendPersistentNotifications`, `assignSellerAdminNotification`, `persistSuperAdminNotification`, and `logActivitySafely` (linked fan-out). If you already wrote the inbox item, set `skipLinkedNotification: true` on the activity log to avoid duplicates.

Never ship a Super Admin ↔ seller feature without both-direction, persistent notifications.
